":"solteiro","p":"adj","fem":"solteira","ipaBR":"/sowˈte(j).ɾu/","ipa":"/sowˈte(j).ɾu/","ipaPT":"/solˈtɐj.ɾu/","gl":"single","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"roa-opt","f":"solteiro","t":"inh"},{"l":"la","f":"sōlitārius","t":"inh","g":"lonely"}],"text":"From Old Galician-Portuguese solteiro, solteyro, from Latin sōlitārius (“lonely”). Compare Spanish soltero, Catalan solter. Doublet of solitário. Folk etymology connects it to solto (“free, unbound”)."}}}}}